# Docker build-context filter for the engine containers whose image_build_context is the repo root
# (convert, discovery, file-repair, ocr, recovery, search — see each Worker's wrangler.jsonc; the
# rest build with their own directory as the context and read the .dockerignore beside it, not this
# one). A .dockerignore is read from the build-context root, so an engine container that builds on
# the crates/ workspace needs this file HERE, not beside its Dockerfile. Allowlist only the source
# the engine images copy — the Rust workspace and the container hosts — so .git, secrets
# (.dev.vars), node_modules, and every package's build output never transit to the builder. Each
# Dockerfile still COPYs only its own subset.
*
!crates
!containers
# Never ship build output even from the allowlisted trees.
**/target
**/node_modules
